@* A glyph centred on its own soft tile — the mark that leads a stat tile, a launchpad card, a
   panel that is asking for something, a scenario's row, an empty page.

   Twelve of these were spelled out by hand and had come apart in the way a box-and-glyph pair
   always does when the two are chosen separately: the same 28px tile carried a 16px icon in the
   dashboard's attention panel and a 14px one in the statistics scenario table, and the six
   utilities that centre the glyph were written in four different orders. The ladder below pairs
   box, corner and glyph once, so two chips of one size cannot drift again.

   The tone is the caller's — jade by default, amber while a panel is asking for something, ink
   where the chip is a handle rather than a subject — because the tone is what the chip is
   saying. It is its own parameter rather than riding on Class: while the two shared one, a host
   that only wanted a margin had to restate the default jade to get it, and the empty page did.

   LetterTile is this component's sibling for a subject identified by a letter rather than a
   glyph; ColorDot for one identified by nothing but its colour. *@

<span class="@BoxClasses inline-flex shrink-0 items-center justify-center @Tone @Class">
    <Icon Name="@Name" Class="@GlyphClass"/>
</span>

@code {
    /// <summary>The glyph — an <see cref="Icon"/> name.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public string Name { get; set; } = "";

    /// <summary>
    /// "xs" a list row's marker, "sm" a table row's, "md" a disclosure's handle, "lg" (default) a
    /// stat tile's or a launchpad card's, "xl" the head of a dialog or an invitation, "2xl" a
    /// landing-page feature, "3xl" the mark over an empty page.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter] public string Size { get; set; } = "lg";

    /// <summary>The fill and the glyph's colour. Jade unless the chip is saying something else.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string Tone { get; set; } = "bg-accent-50 text-accent-700";

    /// <summary>Whatever else the host lays the chip out with — a margin, a hover the card
    /// around it drives.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? Class { get; set; }

    private string BoxClasses => Size switch
    {
        "xs"  => "h-6 w-6 rounded-md",
        "sm"  => "h-7 w-7 rounded-lg",
        "md"  => "h-8 w-8 rounded-lg",
        "xl"  => "h-10 w-10 rounded-xl",
        "2xl" => "h-11 w-11 rounded-xl",
        "3xl" => "h-14 w-14 rounded-2xl",
        _     => "h-9 w-9 rounded-lg", // "lg"
    };

    private string GlyphClass => Size switch
    {
        "xs" or "sm" => "w-3.5 h-3.5",
        "xl" or "2xl" => "w-5 h-5",
        "3xl" => "w-6 h-6",
        _     => "w-4 h-4", // "md", "lg"
    };
}
